**Date added:** 2026-06-28
**Status:** Complete

**Context:** Added after the repo received its first C++ build layer — the `oil_volume_cpp` extension exposing `rolling_mean(values, window)` via pybind11 + scikit-build-core.

**Files:**
- Lesson: [lessons/0001-pybind11-cmake-extension.html](lessons/0001-pybind11-cmake-extension.html)
- Drill: [drills/0001-pybind11-cmake-extension.html](drills/0001-pybind11-cmake-extension.html)
- Vocab: [vocab/0001-pybind11-cmake-extension.html](vocab/0001-pybind11-cmake-extension.html)

**Key concepts covered:**
- Why C++ extensions in a Python trading system (performance, memory layout, SIMD, GIL release)
- How pybind11 works: PYBIND11_MODULE macro, type casters, py::arg, return_value_policy
